Changed `src/queue.ts` to run jobs sequentially in push order via a `#tail` promise chain — jobs start only in a continuation (never synchronously in `push`), failures are recorded in `errors` without stopping later jobs, and `drain` loops until the tail settles so jobs pushed while draining are included; `push` stays synchronous returning nothing. Added tests in `src/queue.test.ts` for ordering/no-overlap, no sync start, error capture, drain-while-pushing, and void return.

